PVD("kiribati_ndp_2016-2019",{"docs":["","KIR NDP 2016 2019"],"s":{"1":[[1,"33","2","Private Sector Development Strategy","This strategy intends to create an enabling environment for private sector growth by reviewing outdated business laws and to effectively implement the enacted business related laws to support the establishment of new businesses and overall growth of the private sector in Kiribati.",""],[1,"34","6","Private Sector Development and Business Law Reform","Promotion of private sector development including enhancing opportunities for external investors and reform of business law to create a conducive business environment.",""],[1,"34","7","Alternative Business Financing Mechanisms","Strengthen and implement alternative business financing mechanisms to improve access to finance especially for Small and Medium-sized Enterprises as envisaged in the Private Sector Development Strategy.",""],[1,"34","8","Integrated Investment Policy Framework","Formulate and effectively implement an Integrated Investment Policy Framework that supports the government business reform agenda and improves foreign investment opportunities in Kiribati.",""],[1,"34","8","Business Law Reform for Ease of Doing Business","Specifically, business law reform will improve the ease of doing business in Kiribati.",""],[1,"36","15","Investment Policy Framework Implementation","Implementation of an Investment Policy Framework.",""],[1,"60","4","Overseas Employment Promotion Policy","Support policies to raise income levels through various means including enhancing overseas employment opportunities to promote stronger growth in remittances; increasing domestic production especially in the Outer Islands through strengthening existing industries and promoting new industries to boost domestic and external trade levels",""],[1,"60","4","Domestic Industry Strengthening and New Industry Promotion","Support policies to raise income levels through various means including enhancing overseas employment opportunities to promote stronger growth in remittances; increasing domestic production especially in the Outer Islands through strengthening existing industries and promoting new industries to boost domestic and external trade levels",""],[1,"60","6","Private Sector Development and External Investment Promotion","Promotion of private sector development including enhancing opportunities for external investors.",""],[1,"60","9","Products and Export Diversification Strategy","To provide sustainable development of sectors where Kiribati has a comparative advantage such as fisheries and coconuts through the implementation of products and export diversification strategies",""],[1,"60","14","National Trade Policy Framework Development","Development of a National Trade Policy Framework",""]],"2":[[1,"27","16","Government Workforce Capacity Building Programme","Strengthening Government's workforce capacity to meet the demands for the Government's services through training programs for employees.",""],[1,"48","5","Public Service Capacity and Delivery Improvement","More work is required to lift capacity in the management and delivery of public service programs.",""],[1,"48","5","Public Financial Management Training Programme","Training needs to be undertaken to raise public financial management standards and productivity levels more generally.",""],[1,"59","11","Government Workforce Training Programme","Strengthening Government's workforce capacity to meet the demands for the Government's services through training programs for employees.",""]],"3":[[1,"14","1","Population Implementation Strategy","Kiribati has adopted a Population Implementation Strategy which promotes healthy family concepts and family planning.",""],[1,"14","1","Outer Island Economic and Social Infrastructure Access Improvement","The strategy intends to stem outer island migration by improving access to economic and social infrastructure to the outer islands and ensure that all people of Kiribati can access the associated opportunities.",""],[1,"45","10","Urban Development Policy and Land Planning Strengthening","Improve and strengthen urban development policies and land planning for sustainable urban growth and private sector development.",""],[1,"47","3","Local Council Administrative Capacity and Governance Strengthening","For local government, a range of problem areas are required to be tackled.",""],[1,"47","3","Outer Islands Council Facilities and Equipment Upgrade","Facilities and equipment for councils in the outer islands require upgrading.",""],[1,"68","9","Land Planning Arrangements for Sustainable Urban Growth","Improve land planning arrangements to be able to cater for sustainable urban growth",""],[1,"68","10","Survey and Planning Capacity Strengthening","Strengthened survey and planning capacity, and improvements in GIS and Data management systems",""]],"4":[[1,"8","5","International Development Partnership and Donor Support Mobilization","We call upon the international and donor community therefore to continue to support us in our efforts to accomplish the development aspirations of this KDP.",""],[1,"9","3","Project Alignment Framework for the KDP","All projects that are proposed by Ministries, agencies, NGOs and Island Councils have to be aligned with the principles of the KDP.",""],[1,"9","4","Ministry Strategic Plans","Ministry Strategic Plans (MSPs) for the period 2016-19 are aligned with the KDP and provide the guiding framework for each Ministry to focus on technical, administrative and operational strategic issues.",""],[1,"9","4","Ministerial Operational Plans","Ministerial Operational Plans (MOPs) set out costed activities to progress the MSPs and feed into the budget process for the preparation of the recurrent and development budgets.",""],[1,"12","12","Implementation of International and Regional Commitments","The Government will pursue these commitments in the interest of Kiribati and its citizens, while taking into account national realities, capacities, and respecting national policies and priorities.",""],[1,"12","13","Alignment of National Plan with Global Commitments","Where appropriate, policies in this Plan have been made consistent these global commitments.",""],[1,"12","15","Means of Implementation Mobilization and Institutional Support","Significant attention to mobilising necessary technical capacity, funding (including through development cooperation) and tailoring institutional arrangements to support the achievement of Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) will remain a key focus of Government.",""],[1,"35","3","Aid Coordination and Development Partner Harmonisation Mechanism","Ensuring aid effectiveness through improving aid coordination and donor harmonisation; compiling six monthly KDP Progress Reports and annual Sustainable Development Goals (SDG) Reports; undertaking biennial Development Partners' Forum and biennial UN Joint Strategy Meetings; maintaining a comprehensive database of projects; and providing support for monitoring of development projects.",""],[1,"56","2","Bi-annual KDP Progress Reporting and Quality Assurance Mechanism","The National Economic Planning Office will compile an analytical Progress Report of the KDP national performance on a bi-annual basis.",""],[1,"56","2","Annual SDG Performance Summary Reporting","NEPO will also compile an annual summary report of the national performance of the post 2015 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).",""],[1,"56","3","Mid-Term Review of the KDP","A Mid-term Review of the KDP will be carried out after two and a half years of the Plan's operation.",""],[1,"56","4","Final Plan Evaluation","A final evaluation of the KDP will be conducted after four and half years of the Plan's implementation.",""],[1,"56","5","KDP Monitoring Support and Donor Coordination","Development partners will assist with the process of monitoring the KDP through the provision of relevant reports such as Project Mid-Term Reviews, Project Completion Reports and participation in the regular Donor Coordination meetings.",""],[1,"63","10","Aid Coordination and Donor Harmonisation Mechanism","Ensuring aid effectiveness through improving aid coordination and donor harmonisation;",""],[1,"63","10","KDP and SDG Progress Reporting System","Compiling six monthly KDP Progress Reports and annual Sustainable Development Goals (SDG) Reports;",""],[1,"63","10","Development Partners and UN Joint Strategy Forums","undertake biennial Development Partners' Forum and biennial UN Joint Strategy Meetings;",""],[1,"63","10","Comprehensive Project Database","maintain a comprehensive database of projects;",""],[1,"63","10","Development Project Monitoring Support","providing support for monitoring of development projects.",""]],"5":[[1,"70","3","Police Service Improvement Programme","Improvements to the police service including response levels; correction skills; the proper maintenance of records; data collection; analysis and reporting; intelligence gathering and analysis through the establishment of a Command centre; discipline and ethical standards; investigation and prosecution skills and case management; community dispute resolution and crime prevention; addressing domestic violence.",""]],"6":[[1,"49","3","Implementation of Ratified International Conventions","Obligations for the reporting and implementation of international conventions that have been ratified need to be met.",""],[1,"49","5","Monitoring of International Convention Obligations","Continue to actively monitor the implementation and reporting of Kiribati's obligations under ratified international conventions including the Human Rights Convention, the Convention on the Elimination of all forms of Discrimination against Women (CEDAW), the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, the Convention on the Rights of the Child, and the Convention Against Corruption.",""],[1,"70","6","Convention Compliance Monitoring Mechanism","Meet and monitor the implementation of Kiribati's obligations under ratified international conventions including the Human Rights Convention, the Convention on the Elimination of all forms of Discrimination against Women (CEDAW), the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, the Convention on the Rights of the Child, and the Convention Against Corruption",""]],"7":[[1,"17","11","VAT and Excise Tax Introduction","The introduction of the VAT and excise taxes will broaden the revenue base and put Kiribati on a more equal footing with the tax structures of other Pacific nations.",""],[1,"18","2","Debt Policy Reform","A debt policy has also been introduced to strengthen decision-making processes and avoid expensive commercial borrowing.",""],[1,"34","10","Tax and Customs Revenue Enhancement Measures","Increase taxation and customs revenue through a range of initiatives including increasing the quality of VAT returns; reducing business and company tax arrears through better compliance and record keeping; self-assessment for business and company tax; and reviewing customs regulations.",""],[1,"34","11","Public Financial Administration Efficiency Reform","Establish effective financial public administration including improvements in the forecasting of taxation revenue and expenditure for the annual budget; and conducting reviews of internal processes to raise efficiency.",""],[1,"34","12","Debt Management Control and Compliance Mechanism","Establish effective debt management controls including ensuring debt levels are sustainable; and monitoring and ensuring that the debt management policy is adhered to.",""],[1,"35","5","Sovereign Wealth Fund Management Enhancement","Enhance management of the sovereign wealth fund, the Revenue Equalisation Reserve Fund (RERF), through monitoring the performance of RERF asset managers and the efficient utilisation of RERF assets.",""],[1,"36","8","Taxation and Customs System Improvement","Increase taxation revenue through improvements to the taxation and customs systems particularly through better compliance measures.",""],[1,"36","10","Effective Debt Management Controls","10. Establish effective debt management controls.",""],[1,"36","14","Sovereign Wealth Fund Management Enhancement","Efficient utilisation of the Sovereign Wealth Fund (the Revenue Equalisation Reserve Fund) and enhancements in its management.",""],[1,"61","19","Tax and Customs Revenue Enhancement Measures","Increase taxation and customs revenue through a range of initiatives including increasing the quality of VAT returns; reducing business and company tax arrears through better compliance and record keeping; self-assessment for business and company tax; and reviewing customs regulations.",""],[1,"61","20","Taxation and Customs Compliance Improvement Measures","Increased taxation revenue through improvements to the taxation and customs systems particularly through better compliance measures.",""],[1,"62","3","Public Financial Administration Efficiency Reform","Establish effective financial public administration including improvements in the forecasting of taxation revenue and expenditure for the annual budget; and conducting reviews of internal process to raise efficiency.",""],[1,"62","5","Debt Management Control and Compliance Mechanism","Establish effective debt management controls including ensuring debt levels are sustainable; and monitoring and ensuring that the debt management policy is adhered to.",""],[1,"62","7","Sovereign Wealth Fund Management Enhancement","Enhance management of the sovereign wealth fund, the Revenue Equalisation Reserve Fund (RERF), through monitoring the performance of RERF asset managers and the efficient utilisation of RERF assets",""],[1,"62","8","Sovereign Wealth Fund Management Enhancement","Efficient utilisation of the Sovereign Wealth Fund (the RERF) and enhancements in its management.",""]],"8":[[1,"49","3","Support for Strong Families, Youth, and Violence-Free Communities","Strong active families and communities, healthy confident young people and children, violence free communities, and access to services for the vulnerable is important for the social growth of the nation.",""],[1,"49","6","Kiribati National Disability Policy Finalisation and Launch","Finalisation and Launching of the Kiribati National Disability Policy.",""],[1,"49","7","Kiribati Shared Implementation Plan on Eliminating Sexual and Gender Based Violence","Execution of the Kiribati Shared Implementation Plan on eliminating Sexual and Gender Based Violence.",""],[1,"49","8","Implementation Support for the Children, Young People and Family Welfare Act","Support the implementation plan of the Children, Young People and Family Welfare Act 2013 to strengthen the roles of the family Institution as a way to minimize and prevent social issues.",""],[1,"49","9","Revised National Youth Policy Formulation","Formulation of a revised National Youth Policy 2017 to 2021.",""],[1,"49","10","National Gender Equality and Women's Development Policy Finalization and Implementation","Finalisation and implementation of the National Gender Equality and Women's Development Policy.",""],[1,"49","11","Women's Economic Empowerment Training and Trainer Manual Development","Improvements in the economic empowerment of women through the conduct of Women's Economic Empowerment Training and the development of a manual on Women's Economic Empowerment for trainers.",""],[1,"50","6","Finalization of the Kiribati National Disability Policy","Finalisation of the Kiribati National Disability Policy.",""],[1,"50","8","Community Outreach Programs on Parenting Skills and Social Welfare","Endorsement of the Implementation Plan of the Community Outreach Programs on Parenting Skills and Social Welfare.",""],[1,"69","9","Finalisation and Launch of the Kiribati National Disability Policy","Finalisation and Launching of the Kiribati National Disability Policy",""],[1,"69","14","Community Outreach Programs on Parenting Skills and Social Welfare Implementation Plan","Endorsement of the Implementation Plan of the Community Outreach Programs on Parenting Skills and Social Welfare.",""],[1,"69","17","Finalisation and Endorsement of National Gender Equality and Women Development Policy","Finalisation and Endorsement of National Gender Equality and Women Development Policy.",""]],"9":[[1,"18","15","Diabetes Prevention and Management Initiatives","Initiatives to prevent and manage diabetes have commenced in South Tarawa.",""],[1,"41","5","NCD Risk Reduction and Prevention Programme","Strengthen initiatives to reduce the prevalence of risk factors for NCDs, and to reduce morbidity, disability and mortality from NCDs through tobacco and alcohol control, healthy eating and physical activities.",""],[1,"41","5","Cancer and Noncommunicable Disease Early Detection and Treatment Programme","prevention, detection and early treatment of cervical cancer, hypertension, heart disease, chronic lung disease, diabetes will be pursued.",""],[1,"64","7","Tobacco and Alcohol Control and Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","NCDs through tobacco and alcohol control, healthy eating and physical activities.",""],[1,"64","7","Early Detection and Treatment of Non-Communicable Diseases","prevention, detection and early treatment of cervical cancer, hypertension, heart disease, chronic lung disease, diabetes will be pursued.",""]],"10":[[1,"18","18","Kiribati Internship Training Program","Formal training under the Kiribati Internship commenced at the beginning of 2014.",""],[1,"19","6","Nursing Scholarship Support through TVET Programme","There has been an increase in scholarships for nurses through the TVET programme to support nursing skills upgrades.",""],[1,"41","10","Health Service Delivery Expansion and Efficiency Improvement","Improve the effectiveness and efficiency of health service delivery, including through expanding hospitals and clinics to meet demand; develop a formal asset maintenance and replacement programme for infrastructure and equipment; and improve procurement and supply of essential medical products, vaccines and technologies.",""],[1,"65","8","Health Service Delivery Expansion and Asset Maintenance Programme","Improve the effectiveness and efficiency of health service delivery, including through expanding hospitals and clinics to meet demand; develop a formal asset maintenance and replacement programme for",""]],"11":[[1,"45","7","Biodiversity Protection and Biosecurity Strengthening","Biodiversity protected though the identification of pest and disease problems, development and promotion of control methods, and strengthened capacity to respond to pest problems including enhanced border security.",""]],"12":[[1,"67","14","Pest and Disease Control Capacity Strengthening","Biodiversity is protected though the identification of pest and disease problems, development and promotion of control methods, and strengthened capacity to respond to pest problems including enhanced border security.",""],[1,"68","4","Biosecurity Legislation Management and Enactment","management and enactment of biosecurity legislation.",""]],"13":[[1,"34","4","Employment Creation through Crewing and Fisheries Development","Create employment opportunities through crewing arrangements with shipping companies and establishment of onshore development of fisheries resources.",""],[1,"34","5","Fishery and Catch Management Data Strengthening","Strengthen fishery and catch management data.",""],[1,"36","5","Fisheries License Fee Revenue Enhancement Measures","Improve revenue through fisheries license fees through advocating the development of measures in PNA, FFA and WCPFC that will improve economic benefits from tuna for Kiribati while conserving the tuna stock.",""],[1,"36","6","Crewing Arrangement Employment Creation","Employment opportunities created through crewing arrangements with shipping companies and establishment of onshore development of fisheries resources.",""],[1,"36","6","Onshore Fisheries Resource Development","Employment opportunities created through crewing arrangements with shipping companies and establishment of onshore development of fisheries resources.",""],[1,"36","7","Integrated Fisheries Information Management System","Establish an integrated fisheries information management system.",""],[1,"61","6","Fisheries License Fee Revenue Enhancement Measures","Improve revenue through fisheries license fees through advocating the development of measures in PNA, FFA and WCPFC that will improve economic benefits from tuna for Kiribati while conserving the tuna stock",""],[1,"61","8","Employment Creation through Crewing Arrangements and Onshore Fisheries Development","Creation of employment opportunities through crewing arrangements with shipping companies and establishment of onshore development of fisheries resources",""],[1,"63","7","Fishery and Catch Management Data Strengthening","Strengthen fishery and catch management data",""]],"14":[[1,"15","4","South Tarawa Sanitation Improvement Sector Project","South Tarawa Sanitation Improvement Sector Project has commenced.",""],[1,"15","4","Water Resource Management and Supply Efficiency Improvement","Water resource management and supply efficiency are being improved on S Tarawa, Kiritimati and outer islands.",""],[1,"21","9","Fragile Water Resources Protection and Freshwater Supply Improvement","The protection of fragile water resources and improvement of fresh water supply has been supported under the coordinated efforts of the World Bank funded Kiribati Adaptation Program Phase III ($10.8 million), Kiriwatsan and the USAID/SPREP support to climate change adaptation initiative.",""],[1,"21","10","South Tarawa Sanitation Improvement Sector Project","The ADB/Australia South Tarawa Sanitation Improvement Sector Project ($23.7 million) will see the rehabilitation of South Tarawa's sewer network, saltwater system and ocean outfalls, as well as hygiene awareness programs.",""],[1,"40","4","Strengthen Targeted Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Programs","Targeted programs need to continue and be strengthened and water quality results need to be monitored more closely and published.",""],[1,"51","2","Rainwater Harvesting Expansion","The rain water harvesting system that is promoted and implemented in Kiribati by the Kiribati Adaptation Project Phase III, Water and Sanitation in Outer Islands (Kiriwatsan) and IFAD projects take into aims to increase the quantity of water available during the wet seasons.",""],[1,"51","2","Simple Hand Pump Groundwater Improvement","The use of simple hand pump system is also promoted as an option to improve the quality and quantity from ground water lens.",""],[1,"51","2","Solar Desalination Development","There is an expectation that the use of solar desalination could be a medium term solution for improving the quality and quantity of water from the ground.",""],[1,"51","3","Outer Islands Water and Sanitation Infrastructure Project","Water and Sanitation infrastructure to be built in the outer islands need to be easily maintained through building local communities' sense of ownership and capacities.",""],[1,"51","3","Community Engagement for Water and Sanitation Project Implementation","The engagement and involvement of the communities during the implementation of the project is one of the options to encourage this sense of ownership and assist them improve their ability to maintain the installed systems in the long term.",""],[1,"51","4","Kiritimati Island Water System Improvement","Improvement of the water system in Kiritimati Island is progressing under Secretariat of the Pacific Community supervision and funding by the European Union.",""],[1,"54","3","Safe Water and Sanitation Programme","Promote and implement the use of safe water from ground and water harvesting and sanitation programmes including the following:",""],[1,"54","7","Kiritimati Water Supply Project Completion","Support the completion of the Kiritimati Water Supply project.",""],[1,"54","8","Community Water Security Improvement Programme","Improve water security for communities through development of water supplies from ground resources and rainwater harvesting, and explore use of solar-powered seawater desalination by reverse osmosis.",""],[1,"55","8","Kiritimati Water System Improvement","Improve the water system in Kiritimati Island.",""],[1,"65","4","Safe Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene Access Initiative","new initiatives will be pursued to increase access to, and use of, safe water and basic sanitation services, and promote improved hygiene.",""]],"15":[[1,"15","4","Kiribati Aviation Investment Project","Kiribati Aviation Investment Project commenced.",""],[1,"21","3","Kiribati Aviation Investment Project","The Kiribati Aviation Investment Project ($29.6 million) will provide upgrades to the runways and airport facilities on Tarawa and Kiritimati islands and reform airport management, funded by the World Bank, New Zealand and Taiwan.",""]],"17":[[1,"16","11","Teacher Qualification and Certification Improvement Initiatives","On-going initiatives are in place to improve this situation.",""],[1,"22","5","Teacher Professional Development Support","The Government has placed emphasis on increased skills and capacity of teachers.",""],[1,"22","5","Teacher Registration Regulations","The proposed introduction of regulations for teacher registration will enhance this move towards professional development.",""],[1,"26","3","Curriculum Strengthening and Extension into JSS","This has been accompanied by strengthening of the curriculum, now being extended into JSS",""],[1,"26","3","Teacher Skills and Professionalism Development","and by a strong emphasis on developing both the skills and professionalism of teachers",""],[1,"26","3","Educational Leadership Initiative","These emphases will continue into the next planning cycle and will be accompanied by a major initiative in educational leadership.",""],[1,"26","4","English Language Skills Strengthening Initiative","Initiatives to strengthen English language skills will continue, especially for those students who wish to further their education at overseas institutions and for those teachers seeking professional registration.",""],[1,"26","5","School Learning Environment Infrastructure and Maintenance Programme","Investment in associated infrastructure and resources is necessary to foster a conducive learning environment where students are physically and emotionally safe will continue, ensuring that all students have access to the basic facilities and resources needed to achieve improved learning outcomes.",""],[1,"26","7","Early School Engagement Promotion","Lift enrolment and participation of 6 year olds in Year 1substantially through promotion of successful early engagement in learning as a critical foundation for further learning.",""],[1,"27","1","Teacher Skills Development for Primary Literacy and Numeracy","Establish a more explicit and sustained focus on the teacher skills needed to transform literacy and numeracy achievement levels in Primary School.",""],[1,"27","2","Teacher Skills Development and Registration Reform","Support skills development amongst teachers and increasing the professionalism of each teacher through lifting teacher competencies to meet internationally recognized Teacher Service Standards and implement the Teacher Registration Process as part of strengthening professionalism.",""],[1,"27","3","Transition to English in Primary and Junior Secondary School","accelerate the transition into English in Primary and Junior Secondary School.",""],[1,"27","4","National Curriculum and Assessment Framework Implementation","Priority will be given to the further implementation of the National Curriculum and Assessment Framework, setting of national benchmarks, providing curriculum resources and writing of a new syllabus.",""],[1,"27","5","ICT Curriculum and School Operations Integration Strategy","Implement a strategy to integrate emerging developments in ICT into curriculum and school operations.",""],[1,"27","6","School Rehabilitation Program Refocusing","Provide healthy and safe school buildings and facilities by reviewing and refocussing the school rehabilitation program in consultation with the Facilities Management Unit and stakeholders.",""],[1,"27","7","Primary and Junior Secondary School Facilities Maintenance Funding","Secure ongoing funding for the delivery of the Primary School and Junior Secondary School (JSS) facilities maintenance schedule.",""],[1,"27","8","Inclusive Education Policy Implementation","Effectively implement the Inclusive Education Policy to target children with disabilities and communicate and gain community acceptance of the policy of mainstreaming children wherever appropriate.",""],[1,"27","8","Teacher Capacity Strengthening for Inclusive Education","Also strengthen teacher capabilities to teach to more diverse learning needs and design and develop a supportive and enabling operational environment.",""],[1,"27","9","Education Act Regulatory Implementation","Complete and implement the regulations flowing from the Education Act 2013.",""],[1,"27","11","Collaborative Mechanisms for Ministry of Education Engagement","Strengthen further collaborative mechanisms for MoE engagement with government agencies and other non-government education sector stakeholders.","MoE"],[1,"57","10","Transition to English in Primary and Junior Secondary School","accelerate the transition into English in Primary and Junior Secondary School",""],[1,"57","12","National Curriculum and Assessment Framework Implementation","further implementation of the National Curriculum and Assessment Framework, setting of national benchmarks, providing curriculum resources and writing of new syllabuses",""],[1,"57","12","ICT Integration Strategy for Curriculum and Schools","Implement a strategy to integrate emerging developments in ICT into curriculum and school",""],[1,"57","15","School Rehabilitation Program Refocusing","Provide healthy and safe school buildings and facilities by reviewing and refocussing the school rehabilitation program in consultation with the Facilities Management Unit and stakeholders.",""],[1,"57","18","Primary and Junior Secondary School Facilities Maintenance Funding","Secure ongoing funding for the delivery of the Primary School and Junior Secondary School (JSS) facilities maintenance schedule",""],[1,"58","3","Education Act Regulations Implementation","Complete and implement the regulations flowing from the Education Act 2013.","MoE"],[1,"58","3","Education Sector Collaboration Mechanisms","Establish collaborative mechanisms for MoE engagement with government agencies and other non- government education sector stakeholders.","MoE"],[1,"58","3","Primary School Teacher Skills Strengthening","Establish a more explicit and sustained focus on the teacher skills needed to transform literacy and numeracy achievement levels in Primary School.",""],[1,"58","4","Teacher Skills Development and Registration Reform","Support skills development amongst teachers and increasing the professionalism of each teacher through lift teacher competencies to meet internationally recognized Teacher Service Standards and implement the Teacher Registration Process as part of strengthening professionalism",""],[1,"58","6","Inclusive Education Policy Implementation","Effectively implement the Inclusive Education Policy to target children with disabilities and communicate and gain community acceptance of the policy of mainstreaming children wherever appropriate.",""],[1,"58","6","Teacher Capacity Strengthening for Inclusive Education","Strengthen teacher capabilities to teach to more diverse learning needs and design and develop a supportive and enabling operational environment.",""],[1,"58","8","Early Childhood Education Development Support","Foster the development of early childhood education through support for the development of an",""]],"18":[[1,"16","14","Auspice Agreement for Australian Accreditation of KIT Courses","An Auspice Agreement is operating between the Kiribati Institute of Technology (KIT) and TAFE South Australia resulting in all KIT courses having Australian accreditation, with each course needing to meet the standards within the Australian TVET Quality Framework.",""],[1,"27","12","TVET Quality Standards Strengthening and Accreditation","Strengthen and enforce TVET quality standards so that TVET providers meet regional and international standards including accreditation of KIT with Pacific Regional Qualification Framework",""],[1,"27","13","TVET Access and Entry Expansion Strategy","Improve access and entry opportunities for I-Kiribati into TVET programmes and qualifications through a range of strategies including the development and implementation of an Outer Island and Kiritimati Island strategy and identify opportunities for skills testing and gap training for existing workers.",""],[1,"27","14","TVET Training Diversification for Industry Needs","Diversification of TVET training to match industry needs.",""],[1,"27","15","KIT Bikenibeu Campus Rehabilitation","Rehabilitation of KIT Bikenibeu Campus",""],[1,"59","6","TVET Quality Standards Strengthening and Accreditation","Strengthening and enforcing TVET quality standards so that TVET providers meet regional and international standards including accreditation of KIT with Pacific Regional Qualification Framework",""],[1,"59","6","Expanded Access to TVET for I-Kiribati Learners","Improve access and entry opportunities for I-Kiribati into TVET programmes and qualifications through a range of strategies including the development and implementation of an Outer Island and Kiritimati Island strategy and identify opportunities for skills testing and gap training existing workers.",""]],"19":[[1,"30","5","Seasonal Worker Recruitment Expansion Strategy","more work, including robust marketing strategies, needs to be undertaken to increase the volume of seasonal workers from Kiribati.",""],[1,"30","5","Financial Literacy Training for Seasonal Workers","Work is also needed on programs such as financial literacy training to ensure that workers can derive the maximum benefits from such schemes.",""],[1,"35","9","International Employment Market Expansion","Expansion of international employment in new and existing markets through improved marketing and recruitment strategies.",""],[1,"36","18","Implementation of the Kiribati National Labour Migration Policy","Implementation of the Kiribati National Labour Migration Policy",""],[1,"36","19","Kiribati Workers' Website Development","Development of Kiribati workers' website",""],[1,"61","10","Implementation of the Kiribati National Labour Migration Policy","Implementation of the Kiribati National Labour Migration Policy",""]],"20":[[1,"34","9","Social Security Mechanisms for Vulnerable Groups","Maintain and build on social security mechanisms to ensure that the most vulnerable, particularly those that suffer from disasters and climate related extreme events, are cared for.",""],[1,"47","4","Village Bank Review and Microfinance Service Improvement","Village Banks have not been operating effectively and require a review to provide the necessary micro finance services to outer islands.",""],[1,"60","17","Social Security Mechanisms Maintenance and Expansion","Maintain and build on social security mechanisms to ensure that the most vulnerable, particularly those that",""]],"21":[[1,"18","11","TB and Leprosy Control Programs","The ongoing delivery and sustainability of the TB and Leprosy Control Programs are on track.",""],[1,"18","12","National Lymphatic Filariasis Control and Morbidity Management Plan","The ongoing National Plan for Lymphatic Filariasis and the management of morbidity caused by the disease has been implemented.",""],[1,"41","9","Communicable Disease Control Program Strengthening","Prevent the introduction and spread of communicable diseases through strengthening existing control programs on TB, Leprosy, and Lymphatic Filariasis.",""],[1,"65","4","Communicable Disease Control Program Strengthening","Prevent the introduction and spread of communicable diseases through strengthening existing control programs on TB, Leprosy, and Lymphatic Filariasis.",""]],"22":[[1,"19","2","National Reproductive Health Policy Implementation","The implementation of Kiribati National Reproductive Health Policy is underway.",""],[1,"41","7","Family Planning Service Expansion","Increase access to and use of high quality, comprehensive family planning services, particularly for women.",""],[1,"41","8","Maternal, Newborn and Child Health Improvement Programme","Improve maternal, newborn and child health through care procedures during pregnancy, delivery and the immediate postpartum period and for the newborn; improve the skills and capacity of maternal care attendants; and improve maternal and child health facilities and equipment.",""],[1,"64","15","Maternal, Newborn and Child Health Care Improvement","Improve maternal, newborn and child health through care procedures during pregnancy, delivery and the immediate postpartum and for the new-born; improve the skills and capacity of maternal care attendants;",""]],"23":[[1,"20","4","Kiribati Shared Implementation Plan for Elimination of Sexual and Gender Based Violence","The Kiribati Shared Implementation Plan is the overarching 4-year framework to operationalize the Elimination of Sexual and Gender Based Violence in Kiribati.",""],[1,"41","11","Standard Operating Procedure for Eliminating Sexual Violence","Improve access to high quality and appropriate health care services for victims of gender based violence and services that specifically address the needs of youth, through implementation of the Standard Operating Procedure of Eliminating Sexual",""],[1,"47","1","Family Violence Reduction Activities","With assistance from development partners, the Government is undertaking many activities aimed at decreasing family violence, increasing physical activity, supporting the elderly and youth, and working on national policies for disability and sport.",""]],"24":[[1,"67","4","Climate Change and Disaster Risk Vulnerability Reduction Programs","Reduce the vulnerabilities to the impacts of climate change and disaster risks through more programs designed to mitigate against climate change and more programs implemented to assist with the adaption to climate change.",""],[1,"67","6","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Measures","Increased measures for the adaptation and mitigation of the effects of climate change including \"soft\" methods such as the planting of more mangroves",""]],"25":[[1,"45","9","National Waste Management Campaign","A national campaign on waste management for a cleaner environment and better crop nutrition though methods such as utilising piggery wastes for composting.",""],[1,"45","13","Waste Management Policy and Pollution Control Measures","Measures to enhance waste management policies and pollution control are adopted.",""],[1,"68","4","National Waste Management Campaign","A national campaign undertaken on waste management for a cleaner environment and better crop nutrition though methods such as utilising piggery wastes for composting",""],[1,"68","13","Waste Management and Pollution Control Measures","Measures to enhance waste management policies and pollution control are adopted",""]],"26":[[1,"19","14","Household Agricultural Production Support","Efforts have been made to maximise and sustain agricultural production (crop and livestock) at the household level to provide adequate fresh and healthy food and increase household income.",""],[1,"45","8","Atoll Soil Management Technology Development and Adoption","Soil management technologies appropriate for atoll conditions developed and adopted.",""],[1,"68","4","Soil Management Technology Development for Atoll Conditions","Soil management technologies appropriate for atoll conditions developed and adopted.",""]],"27":[[1,"53","1","International Airport Upgrade Programme","A major upgrade of the international airports at Bonriki and Cassidy is in progress",""],[1,"53","1","Kiritimati Port Capacity Improvement","Priority now needs to be given to improving the capacity of the port on Kiritimati Island to accommodate regional, fishing and tourism vessels, and the wharves, jetties and airfields on the outer islands.",""],[1,"53","1","Outer Islands Transport Infrastructure Upgrade","Upgrading of Kanton Island airport in the Phoenix islands would support development of tourism potential and the feasibility of establishing an air link between Tarawa and Kiritimati.",""],[1,"53","1","Outer Islands Roads and Causeways Rehabilitation","Intra-island transport and the provision of social services are hampered by the poor condition or lack of roads and causeways on the outer islands.",""],[1,"53","1","Betio Causeway Major Reconstruction","The economically crucial causeway linking the Betio port and business centre to the rest of Tarawa and the Bonriki airport is at high risk of collapse and in urgent need of major reconstruction.",""],[1,"53","5","Environmentally Sustainable Causeway Construction","Implement environmentally sustainable causeways in both the urban and rural areas including the completion of the new causeway between Betio and Bairiki.",""],[1,"53","6","Outer Islands Roads and Airfields Upgrading Completion","Undertake to complete the implementation of the roads and airfields upgrading in the outer islands.",""],[1,"53","7","Line and Phoenix Islands Infrastructure Improvement","Identify and improve the infrastructure needs for the Line and Phoenix islands including the sea port and airport facilities on Kanton Island.",""],[1,"54","10","Kiribati Aviation Investment Project","Improve operational safety and oversight of international air transport infrastructure through the completion of the Kiribati Aviation Investment Project.",""],[1,"54","11","Inter-Island Transport System Improvement","Improve the inter-island transport system.",""],[1,"55","2","Outer Islands Roads and Airfields Upgrading","Complete roads and airfields upgrading on 8 outer islands under Phase 1 and Phase 2 by end of 2019.",""],[1,"55","3","Infrastructure Development Technical Support","Provide technical support for the development and improvement of infrastructure on Kanton Island.",""],[1,"71","3","Infrastructure Development Programme","To improve access to quality infrastructure in urban and rural areas including the development of new infrastructure including water and sanitation, energy, shipping, airports and roads by the year 2019",""],[1,"71","11","Kanton Airfield and Port Facilities Improvement","Improve the Kanton airfield and port facilities",""]],"28":[[1,"21","5","Solar System Maintenance Pricing Mechanism","A pricing system aimed at supporting the ongoing maintenance and improved sustainability of these different systems will be explored.",""],[1,"21","6","Solar Photovoltaic Grid Connection and Rooftop Installation Programme","By 2016 three new solar photovoltaic systems will be connected to the Public Utilities Board (PUB) grid on South Tarawa with an additional peak capacity of 1.4 MW, or 30 per cent of peak demand.",""],[1,"52","2","Solar Photovoltaic Grid Connection and Rooftop Installation Programme","By 2016 three new solar photovoltaic systems will be connected to the PUB grid on South Tarawa with an additional peak capacity of 1.4 MW, or 30 per cent of peak demand.",""],[1,"52","3","Renewable Energy Pilot Trials","Pilot trials of renewable energy options will continue on wind generation, coconut oil biofuel, solar-powered water pumps and hybrid mini-grid systems.",""],[1,"52","4","Solar Power Battery Technology Upgrade","The installation of batteries which adopt new dry cell technologies will assist with the sustainability of power from solar energy.",""],[1,"54","9","Renewable Energy Development and Promotion","Develop and promote the use of renewable energy in all sectors of the economy including the implementation of the Kiribati Integrated Energy Roadmap.",""],[1,"54","16","PUB Medium-Term Reform Plan","Adoption of a medium-term reform plan of the PUB detailing the reform options to achieve operationally and financially sustainable electricity, water, and sanitation services.",""],[1,"55","10","Solar Photovoltaic Systems Connected to the PUB Grid","Three solar photovoltaic systems connected to the PUB grid on South Tarawa by the end of 2016.",""],[1,"55","16","PUB Medium-Term Reform Plan","Adoption of a medium-term reform plan of the PUB.",""],[1,"71","31","Fuel Supply Contract Standardization","Develop and adopt a fuel supply contract based on internationally acceptable standards",""],[1,"72","10","Medium-Term Reform Plan Adoption","Adoption of a medium- term reform plan",""]],"29":[[1,"18","1","Telecommunications Market Liberalization Framework","a framework allowing for a second entrant to the market and for providing services to all outer islands is being established.",""],[1,"46","6","Survey and Planning Capacity Strengthening","Strengthened survey and planning capacity, and improvements in GIS and Data management systems.",""],[1,"54","12","Outer Islands Telecommunications Connectivity Improvement","Facilitate improved telecommunications connectivity for the Outer Islands.",""],[1,"54","14","Ministry Data Storage and Management Upgrade","Upgrade and improve data storage and management and use by staff in Ministries.",""],[1,"54","15","Ministry ICT Capacity Building Programme","Upgrade and enhance the capacity of ministry professional and support staff in the use and application of appropriate levels of competency in the information and communication technology.",""],[1,"61","12","Kiribati Workers' Website Development","Development of Kiribati workers' website",""]],"30":[[1,"20","13","Government Data Disclosure and Publication Initiative","The Government is moving to provide enhanced disclosure and publication of government data to ensure the accountability of government to the community.",""]],"31":[[1,"14","2","Climate Change Adaptation Programs","Kiribati is working with donors to finance adaptation programs which will be vital for a nation with the majority of its land lying just above sea level.",""],[1,"19","16","Coastal Resilience Improvement Measures","Coastal resilience continues to be improved with further construction of seawalls where appropriate, beach enhancement and expanded planting of mangroves.",""],[1,"45","2","Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Programmes","Reduce the vulnerabilities to the impacts of climate change and disaster risks through more programs designed to mitigate against climate change and more programs implemented to assist with the adaptation to climate change.",""],[1,"45","3","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Measures","Increased measures for the adaptation and mitigation of the effects of climate changes including \"soft\" methods such as the planting of more mangroves.",""],[1,"45","12","Investigation of Technical Solutions for Urban Growth and Climate Impacts","Investigation of technical solutions to overcome the problems of urban growth and people affected by climate change.",""],[1,"51","1","Strategic Coastal Protection Initiatives","A priority goal therefore is more strategic coastal protection initiatives including identification of vulnerable areas and introducing robust seawall designs to withstand the impacts of rising seas.",""],[1,"51","1","Mass-Concrete Seawall Replacement","One of the visible efforts in this direction is the total replacement of the \"sandbag\" seawall design with a new \"mass- concrete\" seawall design.",""],[1,"51","1","Climate Change Proofing Policies and Building Codes","Development of and adopting climate change proofing policies and codes for government, public and private buildings are also part of this plan.",""],[1,"53","8","Strategic Coastal Protection Initiatives","Adoption of strategic coastal protection initiatives including identification of vulnerable areas and the introduction of robust seawall designs.",""],[1,"54","1","Environmentally Sustainable Building Design and Construction Policy","Develop policies on environmentally sustainable designs and innovative building construction methods including the application of the Building Codes and full compliance, periodic reviews and update.",""],[1,"55","4","Strategic Coastal Protection Initiatives","Increased number of strategic coastal protection initiatives including the application of mass concrete seawalls.",""]],"32":[[1,"35","2","National Strategy for the Development of Statistics","Enhance the collection and availability of statistics through the implementation of a National Strategy for the Development of Statistics.",""],[1,"35","4","Integrated Project Monitoring System","Promote the use of an integrated project monitoring system in Ministries and SOEs.",""],[1,"36","12","National Strategy for the Development of Statistics","Enhance the collection and availability of statistics through the implementation of a National Strategy for the Development of Statistics.",""],[1,"48","5","National Audit Office Performance Audit Strengthening","The quality of the work of the Kiribati National Audit Office (KNAO) requires improving to be able to undertake performance audits of Ministries and SOEs.","Kiribati National Audit Office (KNAO)"],[1,"56","1","National Strategy for the Development of Statistics","A key strategy of the 2016-19 KDP is the development and implementation of a National Strategy for the Development of Statistics (KPA 2).",""],[1,"56","1","Centralised National Statistical Website","This will include the development of a centralised national statistical website where all statistical information from all Ministries will be stored.",""],[1,"62","14","National Strategy for the Development of Statistics","Enhance the collection and availability of statistics through the development and implementation of a National Strategy for the Development of Statistics.",""],[1,"62","15","National Strategy for the Development of Statistics","Production of a National Strategy for the Development of Statistics.",""],[1,"63","4","National Statistical Data Systems Strengthening","development of a centralised national statistical website; undertaking a Household Income and Expenditure Survey; conducting the analysis of the 2015 Kiribati Population Census; and undertaking a Demographic and Health Survey; improve the data collection and management from Birth, Marriage and Death Registrations and improve the collection of health and education statistics",""],[1,"63","5","Centralised National Statistical Website Development","Development of a centralised national statistical website.",""],[1,"63","8","Integrated Fisheries Information Management System","Establishment of an integrated fisheries information management system",""]],"33":[[1,"47","2","Judiciary Complex Construction and Upgrade","A new complex is needed to cater for Judicial Officers of the High Court and Magistrates' Court, archives for both the High Court and Magistrates' Courts, sheriff's archives, and a library.",""]],"34":[[1,"48","1","Police Service Improvement and Capacity Building Initiatives","These include improvements in service (including customer service) and response level to the community; improvements in police/correction skills, supervision and management; the proper maintenance of station/divisional records to keep track and respond efficiently and effectively to irregularities; improvements in data collection (crime data and clearance rate, hotspots, recidivism, road safety, etc), analysis and reporting to provide accurate trends and informed decision-making; improvements in intelligence gathering and analysis through the establishment of a Command centre and other initiatives to provide real- time information to facilitate more efficient and effective decision-making; improvements in police discipline and ethical standards within the organisation; improvements in investigation and prosecution skills and management of cases; the empowerment of the community through community policing initiatives to participate in dispute resolution and crime prevention; addressing domestic violence, sexual abuse and other crimes impacting on women and children.",""],[1,"48","1","UN Accredited Peacekeeping Training Establishment","there is a need for the establishment of UN accredited training in peacekeeping operations to facilitate ongoing participation in international policing.",""]],"35":[[1,"32","5","State-Owned Enterprise Reform Programme","The program of State Owned Enterprise (SOE) reform, has been embarked upon to improve the financial viability and management of SOE operations.",""],[1,"35","1","State-Owned Enterprise Commercialisation and Rationalisation Programme","Place State Owned Enterprises on a more commercial footing including the completion of the rationalisation of the coconut industry; rationalise at least two other SOEs including activities such as privatization, Public Private Partnerships (PPP), mergers or contracting out services; the production of annual Statements of Intent (SOIs) by all SOEs and the production of timely half yearly and annual reports by all SOEs.",""],[1,"36","11","State-Owned Enterprise Commercialization Reform","Place State Owned Enterprises on a more commercial footing.",""],[1,"62","11","State-Owned Enterprise Commercialisation and Rationalisation Programme","Place State Owned Enterprises on a more commercial footing including the completion of the rationalisation of the coconut industry; rationalise at least two other SOEs including activities such as privatization, Public Private Partnerships (PPP), mergers or contracting out services; the production of annual Statements of Intent (SOIs) by all SOEs and the production of timely half yearly and annual reports by all SOEs.",""],[1,"62","12","State-Owned Enterprise Commercialization Reform","Place State Owned Enterprises on a more commercial footing",""]],"36":[[1,"18","6","Coconut Industry Rationalisation","Rationalisation of the coconut industry has commenced",""],[1,"35","6","National Trade Policy Framework Development","Maximize benefits that arise from trade opportunities through the development of a National Trade Policy Framework to increase supply capacity and create market conditions that link producers with the overseas markets.",""],[1,"35","7","Coconut Sector Development Strategy","The Plan intends to implement products and export diversification strategies through the formulation and effective implementation of a coconut sector development strategy.",""],[1,"35","7","Fisheries Value-Added Investment Support","It also intends to support the effective implementation of fisheries policy by encouraging investment in value added economic activities in the fisheries sector.",""],[1,"36","16","National Trade Policy Framework Development","Development of a National Trade Policy Framework.",""],[1,"36","17","Coconut Sector Development Strategy","Development and Implementation of a Coconut Sector Development Strategy.",""]],"37":[[1,"27","10","Early Childhood Education Legislative and Operational Support","Foster the development of early childhood education through support for the development of an appropriate legislative framework and the development of a supportive operational environment.",""],[1,"41","9","Safe Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene Access Initiative","new initiatives will be pursued to increase access to, and use of, safe water and basic sanitation services, and promote improved hygiene.",""]],"38":[[1,"26","6","National Sport Policy","All strategies to develop and implement national sports at all levels shall be form part of a newly established National Sport Policy.",""],[1,"27","18","National Sport Policy","Establishment, endorsement and implementation of the National Sport Policy.",""],[1,"28","15","National Sport Policy Implementation","The establishment, endorsement, and implementation of the National Sport Policy.",""],[1,"42","2","Sport and Physical Activity Participation Promotion","Improve sport and physical activity participation particularly for youth and people with disabilities as a means of improving health standards.",""],[1,"47","1","Physical Activity Promotion Activities","With assistance from development partners, the Government is undertaking many activities aimed at decreasing family violence, increasing physical activity, supporting the elderly and youth, and working on national policies for disability and sport.",""],[1,"47","1","National Disability and Sport Policy Development","With assistance from development partners, the Government is undertaking many activities aimed at decreasing family violence, increasing physical activity, supporting the elderly and youth, and working on national policies for disability and sport.",""],[1,"47","1","National Youth Policy Review and Update","The National Youth Policy requires review and updating and a more coordinated approach to implementing youth development programs.",""],[1,"47","1","Coordinated Youth Development Programme Implementation","The National Youth Policy requires review and updating and a more coordinated approach to implementing youth development programs.",""]],"39":[[1,"41","6","Road Safety Action Plan","Through the Ministry of Public Works and Utilities, implement a Road Safety Action Plan to ensure that communities enjoy the benefits of improved and safe transport services and that road-related injuries and fatalities are minimised.","Ministry of Public Works and Utilities"],[1,"42","3","Food Safety Act Implementation and Food Standards Establishment","Strengthen the implementation of the Foods Safety Act and establish foods standards to safeguard consumer health and safety",""]],"40":[[1,"21","4","Domestic Roads and Airfields Upgrade Programme","Efforts are in place to improve and upgrade domestic roads and airfields including the outer islands, using funding support from Taiwan.",""]],"41":[[1,"21","8","Steel Fuel Storage Tank Construction Project","A Taiwan funded project is on-going to build two steel fuel storage tanks which will give KOIL a 2,000 mt additional fuel capacity.",""]],"42":[[1,"19","15","Environmentally Sustainable Construction Aggregate Extraction and Processing","Environmentally sustainable extraction and processing of construction aggregates has been established through the enterprise Te Atinimarawa Corporation Ltd (TACL) which began operations in late 2014, dredging, excavating and processing coralline material from the lagoon for commercial supply.",""],[1,"44","2","Sustainable Aggregate Extraction and Alternative Livelihoods Support","the growing demand for building materials on South Tarawa for housing, infrastructure and improving coastal resilience will require concerted efforts to use the sustainably extracted supplies of aggregate dredged from the lagoon and to ensure that those who were reliant on sand-mining find alternative productive livelihoods.",""],[1,"45","14","Sustainable Aggregate Extraction and Processing Compliance Improvement","The viability of sustainable aggregate extraction and processing is maintained and compliance with restrictions on sand-mining is improved.",""]],"43":[[1,"44","6","Nature-Based Tourism Support Infrastructure Investment","nature-based tourism initiatives will require parallel investment in water supply, sanitation, accommodation, energy, transport and telecommunications.",""],[1,"45","11","Outer Islands Nature-Based Tourism Infrastructure Investment","Increasing nature based tourism to the outer islands through investment in water supply, sanitation, accommodation, energy, transport and telecommunications.",""]],"44":[[1,"48","5","Public Sector Service Delivery Improvement","Improvements in service delivery are required for the public sector to be managed more efficiently and capable of responding to community needs.",""],[1,"49","3","Improvement of Ministry Service Quality and Standards","The quality and standards of Ministry services requires improvement to protect and enhance the dignity, rights, safety and welfare of Kiribati people.",""],[1,"49","12","Timely Financial and Performance Audits","Timely financial audits and performance audits of Ministries and SOEs undertaken by the KNAO.","KNAO"],[1,"49","14","Public Service Governance Transparency and Accountability Reform","Improve the public service governance through adopting transparency and accountability in services delivery by Government employees.",""],[1,"70","9","Public Service Transparency and Accountability Reform","Improve the public service governance through adopting transparency and accountability in services delivery by Government employees",""]],"45":[[1,"49","1","Labour Law Administration Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of the Ministry of Labour and Human Resource Development also needs to be strengthened in order to effectively administer the new labour laws to ensure compliance by both Government and private sector.","Ministry of Labour and Human Resource Development"],[1,"50","1","Employment and Industrial Relations Code Implementation and Enforcement","Implementation and enforcement of the Employment and Industrial Relations Code and the Occupational Health and Safety Act.",""],[1,"50","1","Occupational Health and Safety Act Enforcement","Implementation and enforcement of the Employment and Industrial Relations Code and the Occupational Health and Safety Act.",""]],"46":[[1,"49","2","Local Council Trust Fund Establishment","Part of this security could involve the setting up of Trust Funds to enable councils to use interest payments to supplement recurrent spending and for expenditure on development projects.",""],[1,"50","2","Local Council Officer Training Programme","Increased training for Local Council officers.",""]],"47":[[1,"49","4","Review of NGO and Faith-Based Organization Regulatory Framework","Review the Incorporated Societies Act and Religious Bodies Registration legislation and regulations to build a strong NGO sector and support to faith based organisations.",""],[1,"49","13","National Cooperative Policy Development","Development of a National Cooperative Policy to build the capacity of the cooperative movement through diversifying the range of cooperative enterprises, and promotion of good governance, compliance to laws, regulations and standards.",""],[1,"50","3","Village Banks Microfinance Review","Review of the Village Banks to provide micro finance to the outer islands.",""],[1,"50","13","National Cooperative Policy Development","Development of a National Cooperative Policy to strengthen Cooperatives and Credit Unions.",""],[1,"69","7","Village Bank Review for Outer Islands Microfinance","Review of the Village Banks to provide micro finance to the outer islands",""],[1,"69","19","National Cooperative Policy Development","Development of a National Cooperative Policy to strengthen Cooperatives and Credit Unions.",""],[1,"70","8","Review of NGO and Faith-Based Organization Regulatory Framework","Review the Incorporated Societies Act and Religious Bodies Registration legislation and regulations to build strong NGO sector and support to faith based organisations",""]],"48":[[1,"53","2","Line and Phoenix Integrated Development Strategy","A Line and Phoenix Integrated Development Strategy is in progress.",""],[1,"54","18","Line and Phoenix Integrated Strategy Implementation","Commence the implementation of key components of the Line and Phoenix Integrated Strategy.",""]],"49":[[1,"54","13","Professional and Technical Staff Training Programme","Promote training opportunities for professional and technical staff in relevant ministries including work attachments in local and overseas programmes.",""],[1,"54","17","Plant and Vehicle Unit Reform Plan","Identify and implement a medium-term reform plan and options to improve the operations and functionality of the Plant and Vehicle Unit.",""],[1,"72","11","PVU Operational and Functional Improvement","Improve the operational and functionality of the PVU",""]],"50":[[1,"60","11","Coconut Sector Development Strategy","Develop and effectively implement a Coconut Sector Development Strategy",""]]}});